<title>AUSTRIA: OMV to integrate filling station units.</title>
<headline>OMV to integrate filling station units.</headline>
<dateline>VIENNA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Austrian oil and chemicals conglomerate OMV said on Friday it would integrate two of its fully-owned subsidiaries, both of which operate filling stations, into the group in an effort to cut costs.</p>
<p>The company said 120 filling stations currently operated by Stroh and 57 operated by its OTAG unit, with combined sales of about 1.39 billion schillings, would in future be operated by OMV directly, even though they would retain their brand names.</p>
<p>-- Vienna newsroom +431 53112 274</p>
</text>
